  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The angle of deviation through a prism is minimum when&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0168_e1c5e7db535d.png\" style=\"width: 291px; height: 164px;\" /></p><p>(A) Incident ray and emergent ray are symmetric to the prism</p><p>(B) The refracted ray inside the prism becomes parallel to its base</p><p>(C) Angle of incidence is equal to that of the angle of emergence</p><p>(D) When angle of emergence is double the angle of incidence</p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Statements (A),(B)&nbsp;and (C)&nbsp;are true",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Only statement (D) is true",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Only statements (A) and (B) are true",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Statements (B) and (C) are true",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As per the figure given in question, we are considering it an Isosceles Prism.</p><p>Deviation is minimum in a prism when :</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and ray <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is parallel to base of prism.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0168_1ddbd4002c9a.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 160px;\" /></p>"
  }
}